      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2012. Published by Elsevier Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "This article suggests that opportunities to make strategic linkages between health, well-being and sustainable development are missed too often. There is a need for a more sophisticated understanding of the current landscape, which builds on the links between sustainable development, health, well-being and social justice. There is a need for a more sophisticated understanding of health economics to inform policy decisions, ensuring that the impact of mega-externalities (e.g. obesity) are considered and inform planning and policy decisions."
      },
